WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.529
Film Courage: Ken of the many books that you’ve
written (and you have one you co-wrote entitled

00:00:03.529 --> 00:00:08.080
Writing Treatments That Sell and maybe you
can hold it up so people can see it’s cool

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.019
cover there and first off can we define what
is a treatment?

00:00:12.019 --> 00:00:15.360
Dr. Ken Atchity, author/producer: Well, it’s
one of the things that Chi-Li Wong and I looked

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.980
into when we wrote this book because we kept
getting asked that question by clients “What

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:21.980
is a treatment?”

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:25.400
We had to explain it over and over again and
then suddenly it occurred to us “What is

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:26.400
a treatment?”

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.400
ourselves?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:28.410
What is their definition?

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:35.130
So we did a survey of about 30 execs in television
and film and asked them that question “How

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.820
would you define a treatment?”

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:41.550
And we asked them about 10 other questions
and we really based the book on their answers.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:48.250
And so basically the answer is that a treatment
is a relatively brief written pitch written

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.260
story intended to be intended to be dramatized
for motion picture for film or television.

00:00:54.260 --> 00:01:05.850
And it’s written in user-friendly, grammar-free,
quick language that is easy to follow and

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:11.890
it contains highlights the most important
characters events and the obligatory scenes

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:14.880
in the story.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.530
So how long is the treatment?

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:21.930
Relatively brief, three pages to let’s say
15 pages.

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:28.140
Once it’s passed 15, 20 it’s getting no
longer relatively brief.

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.530
There was no industry agreement on it.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:38.360
And basically treatments range from 5 to 10
pages (good treatments) and we recommend that

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:43.740
because of the attention span of who you are
dealing with (the audience), your reader (the

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.740
buyer).

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:50.390
His attention span is limited and you do not
want to extend it because he wont be there

00:01:50.390 --> 00:01:54.420
or she wont be there at the end of the story
if you make it too long.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.659
So that’s basically what a treatment is
and it’s used for two purposes.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:01.870
It diagnoses the faults in the story.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:06.170
So you write a treatment of the story to see
your faults in it, so it’s a diagnostic

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:12.390
tool and then you fix them and then it becomes
a sales tool because people are willing to

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:18.580
read a treatment when they wont read a script
because a script is a serious engagement whereas

00:02:18.580 --> 00:02:21.340
a treatment can be read relatively quickly.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:28.200
And it’s used in every part of the industry
and it’s different from a synopsis because

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:34.900
a synopsis is a dry fully detailed summary
of a story.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:41.180
You’d find a synopsis in a coverage for
example but the treatment is a pitch.

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:45.030
It’s the substitute for a live pitch.

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:50.660
I’m doing a webinar called Pitch Perfect
which is about pitching and when you get the

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.120
rare occasion to do that.

00:02:52.120 --> 00:02:55.870
But now with the Internet, we are going to
do it virtual pitching so that people can

00:02:55.870 --> 00:03:00.500
actually pitch to a producer and get an answer.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:07.080
And a pitch is an extremely fortunate chance
to sell your story.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.630
And again you do not want to be prefacing
it with anything.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:14.220
You don’t want to reveal your personality,
that’s not what it’s about.

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:21.330
You want to just tell how strong your story
is by showing the story and a treatment is

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.510
the best you can do if you don’t have the
opportunity to pitch live.

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:31.000
So the treatment replaces the pitch and is
what most people use and use it through email

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:36.560
and any other method they have to hand a piece
of paper to someone else.

